  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "For each pair of real numbers \\(a \\neq b,\\) define the operation \\(\\star\\) as \\[ (a \\star b) = \\frac{a+b}{a-b}. \\]\n\nWhat is the value of \\(((1 \\star 2) \\star 3)?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(-\\dfrac{2}{3}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(-\\dfrac{1}{5}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "This value is not defined."
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "0"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2005-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "First \\((1 \\star 2) = \\dfrac{1+2}{1-2} = \\dfrac{3}{-1} = -3.\\) Then \\((-3 \\star 3) = \\dfrac{-3+3}{-3-3} = \\dfrac{0}{-6} = 0.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Evaluate the inner operation \\((1 \\star 2)\\) first",
        "\\((1 \\star 2) = \\dfrac{1+2}{1-2},\\) then apply \\(\\star 3\\) to that result"
      ],
